name: Crypto laundering
tagline: "A seeded crypto laundering Link Analysis demo - a peel chain from a hacked wallet, a mixer hop matched by timing and amount and 40 exchange accounts cashing out one cluster's funds, planted among 10 900 invented addresses with benign look-alikes"
description: "The crypto laundering Link Analysis demo as a Space Template, Basic tier, for compliance at a virtual-asset service provider and investigators. Six synthetic feeds (wallet, transfer, cluster_hint, exchange_account, kyc_person, cashout; 12 months landed from 2025-10-01 in data/inbox, the next month in data/staged; 10 900 addresses in an invented syn1 format that cannot match a real chain, 44 500 transfers in the invented assets SYC and SUSD, 3 150 accounts at five invented exchanges) are landed by six Collectors and Pipelines. The crypto_links Job folds them into ONE link Dataset (src, dst, kind, ts, amount, event_date, via) of six link kinds; the crypto_screen_links Job derives the three screens the saved views read. Planted stories (ground truth: tools/gen-la-crypto-data.ground-truth.json; pinned by CryptoLinksJobGoldenTest and tools/gen-la-crypto-data.test.mjs): 412.5 SYC stolen from a hacked wallet in one transfer and moved down an 80-hop peel chain that peels small amounts into 6 exchange deposit addresses; three lots that go through a mixer and come out within 2 hours at 98-99 % of the input, to one exchange account; one common-input cluster paying 40 exchange accounts in unrelated names that all cash out to the same 3 bank accounts. Benign look-alikes that must not join a story: a company payroll wallet whose month-end run has the same chain shape, mixer users with near-miss exits, and an over-the-counter desk paying its customers' own accounts. Three saved views. Basic tier: runs on every edition, Basic included. Advanced tier, in the same template and inert on Basic: Demo Users and roles (config/demo-users.toon, roles.toon: crypto.analyst lead, crypto.manager second approver, crypto.reviewer read-only, crypto.outsider not a member, admin), four-eyes above a fan-out of 2000 and Drafts (link-analysis.toon), the crypto_hack_trace_counts and crypto_hack_trace_alerts Jobs and the Alert Rule crypto_deposit_traced_to_hack (a deposit whose funds trace to a labelled hack within 5 hops: on the shipped data the funds stolen from the one hacked wallet reach 2 exchange deposit addresses within 5 transfers of the theft; the other 4 the peel chain pays lie further down it, the 3 deposits the wallet's owner paid before the theft are not counted and the payroll wallet is never traced; unarmed on Basic). Investigations, members, an Entity List, a Case, a held four-eyes expand and a Draft are runtime state: run `node tools/seed-la-crypto.mjs --apply` on an Advanced or Preview build with Demo Auth. Synthetic data only."
minEdition: basic
icon: heroicons_outline:link
contents[7]: "6 Collectors + Pipelines + Datasets (12 months landed, 1 month staged)", "crypto_links Job + Dataset (6 link kinds, via) and the crypto_screen_links Dataset of three screens", "3 saved views (hack peel chain, mixer hop timing match, converging cash-out)", "3 planted stories with benign look-alikes", "Ground truth and golden tests in the repository", "Advanced tier: 5 Demo Users + role table, four-eyes (inert on Basic)", "Advanced tier: Alert Rule on a deposit traced to a labelled hack within 5 hops (counts Job + evaluate Job, unarmed on Basic)"
